## Why This Is Asked

Tests knowledge of Strategy pattern and runtime extensibility; expects a minimal interface for a router strategy and a registry that supports hot-loading new strategies. It also probes how the router dispatches to handlers asynchronously and resolves potential conflicts when multiple strategies may apply.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern
- Runtime plugin registry
- Decoupled routing logic
- Async dispatch and back-pressure
- Conflict resolution and ordering

## Code Example

```typescript
interface Message { routingKey: string; metadata: any }
interface RoutePlan { queue: string; weight?: number }
interface RouterStrategy { route(msg: Message): RoutePlan[] }

class StrategyRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, RouterStrategy>();
  register(name: string, s: RouterStrategy) { this.map.set(name, s) }
  get(name: string): RouterStrategy | undefined { return this.map.get(name) }
}

class Router {
  constructor(private registry: StrategyRegistry, private active?: string) {}
  route(msg: Message) {
    const strat = this.registry.get(this.active || '');
    return strat?.route(msg) ?? []
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design open extension points with a runtime plug-in mechanism, a common requirement in logging and telemetry stacks.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern
- Registry for runtime extension
- Logging concerns: formatting, escaping, performance
- TypeScript interfaces

## Code Example

```typescript
interface LogRecord {
  level: string;
  message: string;
  timestamp: string;
  [key: string]: any;
}

interface Formatter {
  format(record: LogRecord): string;
}

class PlainFormatter implements Formatter {
  format(r: LogRecord) { return `${r.timestamp} [${r.level}] ${r.message}`; }
}

class JsonFormatter implements Formatter {
  format(r: LogRecord) { return JSON.stringify(r); }
}

class FormatterRegistry {
  private map = new Map<string, Formatter>();
  constructor(defaultName: string, private defaultFormatter: Formatter) {
    this.map.set(defaultName, defaultFormatter);
  }
  register(name: string, fmt: Formatter) { this.map.set(name, fmt); }
  get(name: string): Formatter { return this.map.get(name) || this.defaultFormatter; }
}

class Logger {
  private formatterName: string;
  constructor(private registry: FormatterRegistry, formatterName?: string) {
     this.formatterName = formatterName ?? "plain";
  }
  log(level: string, message: string, meta?: any) {
     const rec: LogRecord = { timestamp: new Date().toISOString(), level, message, ...(meta ?? {}) };
     const f = this.registry.get(this.formatterName);
     console.log(f.format(rec));
  }
}
```

```ts
const reg = new FormatterRegistry("plain", new PlainFormatter());
reg.register("json", new JsonFormatter());
const logger = new Logger(reg, "json");
logger.log("INFO","hello world", { user: "alice" });
```

