## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to combine Strategy and Registry patterns for runtime extensibility. Also probes concurrency safety, tenant isolation, and how policies interact with a core cache.

## Key Concepts

- Strategy pattern for eviction behavior
- Registry pattern for runtime pluggability
- Per-tenant policy assignment and safe swapping
- Concurrency considerations and metrics hooks

## Code Example

```javascript
interface CachePolicy {
  onHit(key: string, meta?: any): void
  onPut(key: string, meta?: any): void
  evictCandidate(): string | null
}

class PolicyRegistry<TPolicy> {
  private store = new Map<string, () => TPolicy>()
  register(name: string, factory: () => TPolicy) {
    this.store.set(name, factory)
  }
  create(name: string): TPolicy {
    const f = this.store.get(name)
    if (!f) throw new Error(`Unknown policy: ${name}`)
    return f()
  }
}
```

